    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T20:46:42Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main e048b103c: cumulative_inscribe_cap_reproduction_1570 passes without a change. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nThe test checks 480 stadium faces on unchanged production code. It uses 16 resolutions, five scales, three rotations, and two offsets. Of these faces, 450 produce accepted fits and 30 are refused. In 282 accepted fits, the draw-in exceeds FIT_TOL. All accepted fits stay within the cumulative 5% per-side cap.\n\nThe command is cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib cumulative_inscribe_cap_reproduction_1570 -- --nocapture.\n\nfit() keeps both centre endpoints fixed. face_overshoot() takes the maximum of zero and radius plus fixed distance terms. Subtracting that overshoot clears those terms in one pass, apart from rounding. I found no later corrective commit. Commit ae0838e51 introduced this calculation.\n\nThe first attempt used an unsupported scale of 1e12. Region construction refused it with OutOfRange before the cap assertion. The valid test uses scales from 0.01 to 10000.\n\nSTOPPED at reproduction. No production change or PR. The claim is released.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
