    "created_at": "2026-11-24T15:10:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T15:10:23Z",
    "body": "Issue sweep: this looks no longer applicable: the second pass in `fit()` cannot shrink the slot width on `upstream/main`. The maintainer decides whether to close it.\n\nIn `crates/motion/src/machining2d/slot_room.rs`, `fit()` keeps `fit.a` and `fit.b` fixed across the `for _ in 0..2` loop. In `crates/motion/src/machining2d/slot_room_face.rs`, `face_overshoot()` returns `max(0.0, r + C)`, where `C` does not depend on `r`. The first pass subtracts `out` from `r`. That step clears the overshoot to zero, up to `f64` rounding. In `crates/geometry/src/geo2d.rs`, `Loop::new` caps coordinates at `COORD_LIMIT` (`1e12` mm). Within that range, `f64` rounding stays below `FIT_TOL` (`0.01` mm). The second pass always stops at `out <= FIT_TOL`. It never shrinks `fit.width` a second time. Total draw-in cannot exceed `INSCRIBE_MAX * w`. No valid `Region` can produce the requested pinning face.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
